# Own-wording spells of Valda's Spire of Secrets (2024), chunk 2. TEXT = {name: [summary, full]}.
TEXT = {
"Aberrate": ["Critical Hits against you become normal hits. After you take damage, a Reaction grants Resistance to that damage type.",
 "Your body turns fluid for 1 minute. Any Critical Hit against you counts as a normal hit. Right after you take damage, you can use your Reaction to gain Resistance to that damage type until the spell ends or until you use the Reaction again to switch to a different type. The Resistance does not cover the damage that triggered it."],
"Aerial Alacrity": ["A willing flying creature can Dash or Disengage as a Bonus Action, hover, and has Advantage on Dexterity checks and saves for 10 minutes.",
 "Pick a willing creature you see within range that has a Fly Speed, natural or granted by magic. For 10 minutes, while it is flying, it can Dash or Disengage as a Bonus Action, it can hover, and it has Advantage on Dexterity checks and Dexterity saving throws."],
"Arc Blade": ["Make a melee or 15-ft ranged spell attack with a weapon using your casting ability. It deals Lightning or weapon damage, plus extra Lightning at higher levels.",
 "Lightning runs along the weapon you cast this with, and you make one attack with it. The attack is either a melee attack or a ranged spell attack with a 15 ft range, and it uses your spellcasting ability for the attack and damage rolls in place of Strength or Dexterity. A ranged attack deals Lightning damage. A melee attack deals Lightning damage or the weapon's usual damage type, your choice. Either way the attack adds Lightning damage at level 5 (1d6), 11 (2d6) and 17 (3d6)."],
"Blood Print": ["Ritual. Wet blood on a surface forms a print unique to its owner. You learn the creature's kind, and two casts can match samples.",
 "Touch wet blood on a surface and it reshapes into a crimson pattern unique to the creature it came from. From the print's general shape you can tell what kind of creature it was, such as Human, Gnoll, Deer or Fire Giant. Pressing paper on the print preserves it. If you cast the spell twice, you can tell whether two blood samples came from the same creature."],
"Card Trick": ["Fling a charged card at a target within 60 ft. Choose a ranged spell attack or a Dexterity save. It takes 1d8 Force damage.",
 "You throw a playing card or tarot card filled with magic at a creature within 60 ft. Choose whether you make a ranged spell attack roll or the target makes a Dexterity saving throw. On a hit or a failed save, the target takes 1d8 Force damage. The damage becomes 2d8 at level 5, 3d8 at 11 and 4d8 at 17."],
"Conjure Cannonball": ["Ranged spell attack within 600 ft: 5d10 Bludgeoning, plus a 5-ft explosion where others make a Dexterity save for half damage.",
 "A cannonball appears in flight at full speed and explodes on impact. Make a ranged spell attack against a target you see within 600 ft. On a hit, it takes 5d10 Bludgeoning damage and the blast spreads in a 5-ft Emanation from it. Every other creature in the Emanation makes a Dexterity save and takes half the target's damage on a failure, nothing on a success. Each slot level above 3 adds 1d10 damage."],
"Cosmic Horror": ["10-ft radius within 60 ft. Wisdom save or 6d6 Psychic and Frightened, half damage on a save. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "For an instant you open a gate to a nightmare realm in a 10-ft-radius Sphere centered on a point you see within 60 ft. Each creature in it makes a Wisdom save. On a failure it takes 6d6 Psychic damage and is Frightened for the duration. On a success it takes half damage and is not Frightened. A Frightened creature repeats the Wisdom save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. Each slot level above 3 adds 1d6 damage."],
"Curse of Aging": ["Touch. Wisdom save or the target ages at ten times the normal rate and has Disadvantage on Strength checks and saves. Lasts until dispelled.",
 "A creature you touch makes a Wisdom save. On a failure it is cursed to wither. While cursed it ages ten times faster, gaining ten days of age for each day that passes, and it has Disadvantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws. The curse lasts until dispelled."],
"Dead Fog": ["10-ft sphere of necrotic fog within 120 ft. Constitution save, 3d6 Necrotic, half on a save. You can add your own HP loss for extra dice.",
 "A 10-ft-radius Sphere of necromantic fog forms at a point you see within 120 ft and lasts for the duration. Strong wind such as Gust of Wind disperses it and ends the spell. The area is Heavily Obscured. Each creature in it makes a Constitution save, taking 3d6 Necrotic damage on a failure or half on a success. When you cast it you can take 10, 20 or 30 Necrotic damage yourself, which ignores Resistance and Immunity. The spell then gains 1d6 per 10 damage you took, up to 10d6 total. As a Magic action you can move the fog 30 ft. A creature also saves when the fog moves into its space, when it enters the fog, and when it ends its turn there, but only once per turn. Each slot level above 3 adds 1d6 damage."],
"Demand": ["For 10 minutes, your next listed Enchantment spell (Charm, Command, Dominate, Geas, Suggestion) gains unlimited range. Ends after one use.",
 "This spell lets you send an Enchantment spell to a target at any distance. For 10 minutes, when you cast Charm Monster, Charm Person, Command, Dominate Beast, Dominate Person, Geas or Suggestion, you change its range to unlimited and this spell ends. Pick a target you know, even if you cannot see it. If the spell needs a spoken command, the target hears it in its mind and knows you sent it if it knows you. The spell crosses any distance and even other planes. If the target is on another plane, there is a 5 percent chance the Enchantment fails with no effect."],
"Elemental Curse": ["Touch. Constitution save or cursed for 1 minute: Vulnerability to a chosen Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning or Thunder type. Concentration.",
 "A spark jumps from your finger into a creature you touch and cracks spread across its skin. The target makes a Constitution save or is cursed for the duration. A cursed target has Vulnerability to one damage type you choose from Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning or Thunder. If it has Resistance to that type, it loses the Resistance instead. If it has Immunity to that type, it has Resistance instead."],
"Eye of Ra": ["Two spell attacks at 60 ft, 1d4 Radiant each. A hit gives the next weapon or unarmed attack against it +1d4, or +1d6 if both beams hit it.",
 "Sunlight beams from your eyes. Make two spell attack rolls at one or two targets within 60 ft. Each hit deals 1d4 Radiant damage, and the next attack roll against that target with a weapon or Unarmed Strike before your next turn starts gets a bonus of 1d4. The bonus is 1d6 if both beams hit the same target. Each beam's damage becomes 2d4 at level 5, 3d4 at 11 and 4d4 at 17."],
"Flawed Reconstruction": ["Touch. A creature regains 3d6 HP but its HP maximum drops by 1d6 (minimum 1).",
 "You stitch the wounds of a creature you touch. It regains 3d6 HP, but the repair is poor and its HP maximum is reduced by 1d6, to a minimum of 1. Each slot level above 1 adds 2d6 healing and 1d6 to the maximum reduction."],
"Force Weapon": ["Melee spell attack within 5 ft for 1d10 Force. The blade lingers and can make one Opportunity Attack before your next turn.",
 "You conjure a blade of force that strikes a creature within 5 ft. Make a melee spell attack. On a hit the target takes 1d10 Force damage. Until the start of your next turn the blade remains, and you can make one strike with it as an Opportunity Attack. You make an extra attack at level 5 (2 attacks), 11 (3) and 17 (4), and the attacks can hit the same or different creatures."],
"Frolicking Fountain": ["5-ft water cube within 120 ft lashes out in 20 ft each turn: Dexterity save, 5d6 Bludgeoning, half on a save. Wisdom save can pin Speed to 0.",
 "A 5-ft Cube of hypnotic swirling water appears in an empty space within 120 ft. When it appears, and as a Bonus Action on later turns, you can have it lash out in a 20-ft Emanation from it. Each creature you choose there makes a Dexterity save, taking 5d6 Bludgeoning damage on a failure or half on a success. When a creature tries to leave the area, you can force a Wisdom save. On a failure its Speed is 0 until the start of its next turn. Concentration, up to 1 minute. Each slot level above 5 adds 1d6 damage."],
"Gahoul's Spectral Scythe": ["Throw a scythe down a 60-ft line: Dexterity save, 6d8 Necrotic, half on a save. It can return next turn and hit again.",
 "You throw a spectral scythe along a Line 60 ft long and 10 ft wide. It stops hovering at the end or before a solid surface. Each creature in the line while it travels makes a Dexterity save, taking 6d8 Necrotic damage on a failure or half on a success. A creature has Disadvantage on the save if the scythe comes to rest in its space. If you are within 120 ft of the scythe at the start of your next turn, it flies back to you along a 10-ft-wide line, and creatures in its path make the save again. Each slot level above 6 adds 1d8 damage."],
"Gravity Well": ["15-ft sphere within 120 ft. Strength save, 5d8 Force and pulled or pushed 15 ft, half damage on a save.",
 "A 15-ft-radius Sphere of gravity forms at a point you choose within 120 ft. Choose whether gravity pulls inward to the center or pushes outward. Each creature in the Sphere makes a Strength save. On a failure it takes 5d8 Force damage and is moved 15 ft toward the center or away from it, as you chose. On a success it takes half damage and is not moved. Each slot level above 3 adds 1d8 damage."],
"Hex: Apathy": ["Cantrip. Charisma save or the target is Indifferent toward creatures you choose that it is Hostile to, until damaged or forced to save. Ends at end of your next turn.",
 "One creature you see within 60 ft makes a Charisma save. On a failure it becomes Indifferent toward creatures of your choice that it is Hostile toward. The effect ends early if the target takes damage or is forced to make a saving throw. When the spell ends at the end of your next turn, its attitude returns to normal."],
"Hex: Decay": ["Cantrip. Constitution save or 1d6 Necrotic (ignores Resistance and Immunity), again at the end of each of its turns until your next turn ends.",
 "One creature you see within 60 ft makes a Constitution save. On a failure it takes 1d6 Necrotic damage, which ignores Resistance and Immunity, and takes it again at the end of each of its turns. The spell ends at the end of your next turn. The damage becomes 2d6 at level 5, 3d6 at 11 and 4d6 at 17."],
"Hex: Evil Eye": ["Cantrip. Wisdom save or the target is Frightened until the end of your next turn.",
 "One creature you see within 60 ft makes a Wisdom save. On a failure it is Frightened until the spell ends at the end of your next turn."],
"Hex: Hobble": ["Cantrip. Strength save or the target's Speed drops to 10 ft until the end of your next turn. A flying target falls unless it can hover.",
 "One creature you see within 60 ft makes a Strength save. On a failure its Speed becomes 10 ft until the spell ends at the end of your next turn. If it is flying, it falls unless it can hover."],
"Hex: Musical Interlude": ["Cantrip. Creatures you choose in a 30-ft Emanation gain 1d6 Temporary HP until the end of your next turn.",
 "With an encouraging speech or song, each creature you choose in a 30-ft Emanation from you gains 1d6 Temporary HP. They last until the spell ends at the end of your next turn, and vanish early for a creature that ends its turn outside the Emanation. The amount becomes 2d6 at level 5, 3d6 at 11 and 4d6 at 17."],
"Hex: Ruin": ["Cantrip. Constitution save or the target has a -2 penalty to AC until the end of your next turn.",
 "One creature you see within 60 ft makes a Constitution save. On a failure it takes a -2 penalty to AC until the spell ends at the end of your next turn. The penalty becomes -3 at level 5, -4 at 11 and -5 at 17."],
"Hex: Vanish": ["Cantrip. You are Invisible until the end of your next turn. Creatures within 20 ft that can hear you know where you are. Ends if you attack, deal damage or cast.",
 "With an old chant you gain the Invisible condition until the spell ends at the end of your next turn. Creatures within 20 ft that can hear you can pinpoint your location for the duration. The spell ends early if you make an attack roll, deal damage or cast a spell."],
"Hunger of the Earth": ["Strength save or a creature within 30 ft is pulled underground: Blinded, Restrained, 4d6 Bludgeoning each turn end. Concentration, 1 minute.",
 "The ground opens under a creature you choose on the ground within 30 ft. It makes a Strength save. On a failure it is pulled underground for the duration. On a success its Speed is 0 until the start of your next turn. A creature underground is Blinded and Restrained, cannot teleport, has Cover against attacks and effects from outside the ground, and takes 4d6 Bludgeoning damage at the end of each of its turns. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the spell on itself on a success. Each slot level above 4 adds one target."],
"Inevitable Boulder": ["An 8-ft boulder (AC 18, 100 HP) chases a target at 60 ft per turn. Dexterity save, 6d10 Bludgeoning and Prone, half on a save. Concentration.",
 "A Large boulder 8 ft across appears in an empty space within 60 ft and rolls after one creature you see. It has AC 18, 100 HP and Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage. At 0 HP it vanishes and the spell ends. At the start of each of your turns it moves 60 ft toward its target. When it enters a creature's space, that creature makes a Dexterity save, taking 6d10 Bludgeoning damage and falling Prone on a failure, or half damage on a success. It also crushes nonmagical objects smaller than itself. If it reaches its target it rolls over it and keeps going until its movement ends or an obstacle larger than itself stops it, and it can roll over the target repeatedly. If you hold Concentration for the full 1 minute, the boulder keeps chasing for up to 1 hour or until you dismiss it, and no longer needs Concentration. When it strikes its target, it vanishes and the spell ends."],
"Intrusive Thought": ["Reaction within 30 ft. Wisdom save or the creature's triggering attack automatically misses.",
 "You cast this as a Reaction to an attack, distorting the attacker's thinking. The target makes a Wisdom save. On a failure, the triggering attack automatically misses."],
"Lashing Tendrils": ["5-ft Emanation of tendrils deals 2d4 Bludgeoning to creatures that enter or end their turn there, once per turn. Concentration.",
 "Grotesque tendrils whip around you in a 5-ft Emanation for up to 1 minute. When the Emanation enters a creature's space, and when a creature enters it or ends its turn in it, you can deal 2d4 Bludgeoning damage to that creature. A creature takes this damage only once per turn. Each slot level above 1 adds 1d4 damage."],
"Mandy's Enchanted Carriage": ["Turn a vegetable into a Large carriage with two quasi-real horses. Seats six, Speed 100 ft, AC 12, 100 HP. Lasts until midnight or 24 hours.",
 "You change a vegetable into a Large magical carriage with reins and two quasi-real horses. It carries six passengers, four inside and two on the driver's seat. Those inside have Cover from outside effects and see out through two windows of force. A creature on the seat controls it. It has Speed 100 ft and travels 10 miles in an hour, or 13 at a fast pace. The carriage and horses count as one object with AC 12 and 100 HP, and the spell ends early at 0 HP. If you cast it where time passes normally, it lasts until the twelfth stroke of the next midnight. Elsewhere it lasts 24 hours. When it ends, occupants are placed in nearby open spaces, the carriage shrinks back to a vegetable and the horses vanish."],
"Mass Skirmish": ["Up to six willing creatures within 60 ft get doubled Speed, ignore Difficult Terrain, and provoke no Opportunity Attacks for 10 minutes.",
 "You boost the mobility of up to six willing creatures you see within 60 ft. For 10 minutes each target has its Speed doubled, is not slowed by Difficult Terrain, and does not provoke Opportunity Attacks."],
"Moment to Think": ["Bonus Action cantrip. Time stops for everyone else. Take one extra Search, Study or Utilize action, but you cannot affect creatures or others' objects.",
 "You briefly freeze time for everyone but yourself. You gain one extra action and can move within your space while no time passes for others. That action can only be Search, Study or Utilize. You cannot affect or damage any creature or any object other than ones you wear or carry. An object that leaves your hand is also frozen in time."],
"Petal Storm": ["10-ft cube of cutting winds within 60 ft: Dexterity save, 2d6 Slashing rising to 4d6 as you move it. Heavily Obscured. Concentration.",
 "Swirling wind fills a 10-ft Cube you see within 60 ft for up to 1 minute. The area is Heavily Obscured, and on later turns you can use a Magic action to move the Cube 30 ft. When it appears, each creature in it makes a Dexterity save, taking 2d6 Slashing damage or half on a success. Each time you move the Cube with a Magic action, the damage rises by 1d6, to a maximum of 4d6. A creature also saves when the Cube moves into its space, when it enters, and when it ends its turn there, once per turn. Each slot level above 2 adds 1d6 to both the base and maximum damage."],
"Pit Trap": ["Hidden 5-ft pit trap within 30 ft, 10 ft deep, for 8 hours. Dexterity save or fall, 1d6 Bludgeoning per 10 ft.",
 "You create a hidden pit trap on an empty ground space you see within 30 ft. Its 5-ft-square lid looks like the surrounding floor. The pit drops 10 ft into an extradimensional space, or into the open space below if there is one. As a Study action, a creature can check the lid with an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC to spot it. When a Large or smaller creature steps on the lid, it swings open and the creature makes a Dexterity save. On a failure it falls and takes 1d6 Bludgeoning damage per 10 ft fallen. On a success it moves to a space next to the lid. Creatures in the pit can climb or fly out as usual. The spell ends 1 minute after a creature falls in, and anything inside is placed at the top. Each slot level above 2 makes the pit 10 ft deeper."],
"Proto-Abjuration": ["Touch. For 10 minutes a creature gains one ward: thorns, Temporary HP, +2 AC and saves, or damage Resistance. Concentration.",
 "A creature you touch gains one of these benefits for 10 minutes. With a level 4+ slot you can choose two. Use the slot level as the spell level in the numbers. Arcane Thorns: when a creature within 5 ft hits the target with a melee attack, the attacker takes Force damage equal to 2d4 plus the spell level. Temporary Hit Points: the target gains 1d10 plus 5 times the spell level in Temporary HP, which vanish when the spell ends. Armored Ward (level 2+ slot): the target gets +2 to AC and saving throws. Damage Resistances (level 3+ slot): the target has Resistance to one of Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning or Thunder, your choice."],
"Proto-Evocation": ["Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder. Single target 2d12 attack within 120 ft, or at level 3+ a cone, line or sphere of 5d8.",
 "You unleash raw elemental energy. Pick Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison or Thunder, then one option. Single-Target: make a spell attack against a creature within 120 ft, dealing 2d12 of the chosen type on a hit. Cone (level 3+ slot): creatures in a 30-ft Cone from you make a Dexterity save, taking 5d8 on a failure or half on a success. Line (level 3+ slot): creatures in a Line 90 ft long and 5 ft wide from you make a Dexterity save, taking 5d8 or half. Sphere (level 3+ slot): creatures in a 15-ft-radius Sphere centered on a point within range make a Dexterity save, taking 5d8 or half. Single-Target damage rises 1d12 per slot level above 1. The area options rise 1d8 per slot level above 3."],
"Psychedelics": ["20-ft Emanation of shifting colors. Creatures you choose have Disadvantage on their next attack roll before your next turn ends. Objects change color for 1 hour.",
 "The colors in a 20-ft Emanation from you swirl into a rainbow. Each creature you choose in it has Disadvantage on the next attack roll it makes before the spell ends at the end of your next turn. Objects you choose within range also change to random, bright, unnatural colors that last 1 hour."],
"Rocks Fall": ["60-ft radius, 120-ft high cylinder within 120 ft. Dexterity save, 10d8 Bludgeoning and buried, half on a save.",
 "Boulders drop from the air in a Cylinder 60 ft in radius and 120 ft high, centered on a point within 120 ft. Each creature in it makes a Dexterity save. On a failure it takes 10d8 Bludgeoning damage and is buried under rubble. On a success it takes half damage and is not buried. A buried creature is Prone and Restrained. It can use an action to make a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC, and on a success it frees itself and ends both conditions."],
"Rusting Grasp": ["Melee spell attack: 6d4 Acid and -3 AC (minimum 10) for 1 hour. Against loose nonmagical metal, destroys a 1-ft cube.",
 "Corrosive acid forms at your fingertips. Make a melee spell attack against a creature or object within reach. On a hit, a creature takes 6d4 Acid damage and has a -3 penalty to AC, to a minimum of 10, for 1 hour. If you target a nonmagical metal object that is not worn or carried, you destroy the parts you choose that fit in a 1-ft Cube. Each slot level above 3 adds 2d4 damage and one extra cubic foot of object destroyed."],
"Secret Enclave": ["Open a 10-ft portal within 60 ft to a 1,000-ft Feywild forest demiplane, tied to a portal key object. Divination cannot find it.",
 "You open a shimmering 10-ft-wide portal within 60 ft that leads to a demiplane, and you enchant an object that fits in a 5-ft Cube to be its portal key. The demiplane is a 1,000-ft Cube resembling a magical Feywild forest, with fertile soil that cannot be burrowed through. The portal in and out opens only while the key is within 60 ft of it. Once made, the portal's location is fixed and it opens only from that place. You or anyone within 60 ft of the portal can open it by casting this spell again. Casting it again also lets you make a replacement or duplicate key. The key and any creature inside cannot be targeted by Divination spells, though Wish can reveal the key's location. You can make Secret Enclaves inside Secret Enclaves only if you made the original demiplane."],
"Sonic Pulse": ["Cantrip within 60 ft. Constitution save or 1d8 Thunder and Deafened. Within 10 ft the damage is 1d10.",
 "You compress a boom into an invisible ball and send it at a creature you see within 60 ft. The target makes a Constitution save. On a failure it takes 1d8 Thunder damage and is Deafened until the start of your next turn. If the target is within 10 ft of you, the spell is amplified and deals 1d10 instead. The damage becomes 2d8 or 2d10 at level 5, 3d8 or 3d10 at 11, and 4d8 or 4d10 at 17."],
"Stone Bones": ["Bonus Action within 30 ft. A creature has Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing until the end of your next turn.",
 "Pick a creature you see within 30 ft. It has Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage until the spell ends at the end of your next turn."],
"Swift Flight": ["Bonus Action touch. A creature gets a 60-ft Fly Speed and can hover until the end of its next turn, then falls if unsupported.",
 "Streaks of energy trace wing shapes on the back of a creature you touch. Until the end of its next turn the target has a Fly Speed of 60 ft and can hover. When the spell ends, it falls if it is in the air and nothing holds it up."],
"Time Hop": ["Bonus Action. Vanish for 1 to 3 rounds and reappear at the start of your turn. While gone you cannot act and nothing affects you.",
 "You jump a few seconds into the future. Choose 1, 2 or 3 rounds. You vanish and reappear after that time at the start of your turn, in the nearest empty space to where you left. While gone you are outside time. You cannot take Actions or Reactions, your Speed is 0, no time passes for you, your spell effects are suspended, and nothing can affect you. With a level 3-5 slot you can choose 1 minute. With a level 5+ slot you can choose 1 hour."],
"Whispering Wind": ["Ritual. Send a message of 25 words or fewer to up to six creatures within 1 mile. Each can whisper a reply to you.",
 "You whisper a message of 25 words or fewer and name up to six target creatures. Each target within 1 mile hears the message on the wind and can whisper a reply that only you hear. The message is blocked to a target if every path to it within range is blocked by solid objects or magical silence."],
"Word of Frailty": ["Bonus Action within 30 ft. Constitution save or the target's AC becomes 10 until the end of your next turn if it was higher.",
 "You speak a withering word at a creature you see within 30 ft. It makes a Constitution save. On a failure its Armor Class becomes 10 until the end of your next turn, if its AC was higher than that."],
}
